-->Use when the conversation is getting long, the avatar seems confused about earlier content, or context needs to be carried across conversations.

## Diagnose

`conversation({ action: "status" })` reports connection and audio state but **not** the transcript — there is no transcript-snapshot tool. Track the conversation from the `transcript.item` events as they arrive on the channel: each carries `item.role`, `item.source`, and `item.text`. `item.source` `"microphone"` is the user; `"assistantAudio"`/`"assistantText"` is the avatar; `"system"` is one of your own injections echoing back (ignore those).

## Subroutines

When the transcript is long, there are two moves. **Reset-and-re-seed is the preferred default** for routine long-conversation hygiene and on topic changes — see [SKILL.md §RESET](../SKILL.md) and [conversation-lifecycle.md](conversation-lifecycle.md).

§SUMMARY_INJECT below is the move when you must preserve the exact running session — an unbroken transcript matters (e.g. the avatar is mid-thought, or recent turns must stay verbatim in context) and only earlier content needs reinforcing. Prefer it only when the live session itself must continue uninterrupted.

### §SUMMARY_INJECT
**When:** the transcript is long or the avatar shows signs of losing context — repetition, confusion, inconsistent recall — **and** the running session must be preserved rather than reset (otherwise prefer reset-and-re-seed, above).
Distil the key facts and decisions so far and inject them as a system message; the avatar uses it as working context going forward.

```
inject({ role: "system", message: "<summary of key points so far>" })
```

### §CONTEXT_REFRESH
**When:** a new conversation should carry forward context from a previous one.
`context`/`topics`/`instructions` are **cleared when a session ends** (reset, reload, close) — they do not carry over. The `agent.deactivate` event tells you what was cleared. To carry context into the next conversation, re-seed it on the next `agent.activate` (or after a reset):

```
set({ context: "<relevant context to carry into the next conversation>" })
```

### §FACT_INJECT
**When:** a specific fact, preference, or decision was established earlier and the avatar seems to have lost track of it.
For a silent, latest-wins correction prefer `set({ context })`. To pin it into the transcript history instead, inject it — keep it short so it's easy to absorb:

```
inject({ role: "system", message: "<specific fact to reinforce>" })
```

## Events

### `transcript.item`
Emitted when a transcript item is finalised.

```typescript
{
  item: {
    id: string;
    conversationId: string;
    role: "user" | "assistant" | "system";
    source: "microphone" | "textInput" | "firstMessage" | "assistantAudio" | "assistantText" | "system";
    text: string;
  };
  createdAt: string;
}
```

### `transcript.delta`
Emitted continuously while a transcript item is streaming (only if you add `transcript.delta` to `VOICE_SERVER_WATCH_TYPES` — it is off by default).

```typescript
{
  conversationId: string;
  itemId: string;
  role: "user" | "assistant";
  source: "microphone" | "assistantAudio" | "assistantText" | "textInput";
  delta: string;
  fullTextSoFar: string;
  createdAt: string;
}
```
